{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739"},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":", with each choice the other way round: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbours. The cost is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": O(m √n) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"title":"Graph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/covering","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","title":"Covering","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()":{"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}]}}}